.TH geectl-remote-add-channels 1  "geectl-remote-add-channels 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-add\-channels \- Add the channels defined for a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the addition. A project or package with no channels defined is a no\-op
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote add\-channels\fR [\fB\-\-enable\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-disabled\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> [\fIPACKAGE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add the channels defined for a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the addition. A project or package with no channels defined is a no\-op
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-all\fR
Enable all added channels including the ones disabled by default. Cannot combine with `\-\-skip\-disabled`
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-disabled\fR
Skip disabled channels: add the channel packages but not their repositories. Cannot combine with `\-\-enable\-all`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to add channels to
.TP
[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
The package to add channels to. Omit for the whole project
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
